{
  "name": "How to Structure Your Content So AI Actually Understands It",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1: Start with Real Questions",
      "text": "Before you write anything, really dig into what questions people are asking. AI Visibility Solutions uses tools like the Perplexity API and analyzes Google Search Console's \"unanswered questions\" to find high-intent queries. Your questions should be exactly what a prospect would type or say, not just a keyword phrase.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2: Use Question-Based Headings",
      "text": "Each section of your content should be framed as a direct question. This acts like a signpost for AI, immediately telling it what information follows. It makes your content modular and easy for AI to parse.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 3: Provide a Direct Answer Up Front",
      "text": "This is critical. The very first sentence or two under your question-based heading needs to provide a concise, direct answer. Think of it as the most important takeaway. The AI should be able to grab this snippet and use it right away.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 4: Add Supporting Details",
      "text": "After your direct answer, you can expand with lists, examples, and short explanations. These details provide context and depth, making your answer more comprehensive, but they come *after* the initial punchy answer.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 4
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 5: Incorporate Rich Schema",
      "text": "This is the language AI systems speak. Every article and FAQ should be output with rich JSON-LD schema (like FAQPage or Article schema). This tells AI exactly what your content is about and how it's structured, boosting its chances of being understood and cited.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 5
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 6: Publish Where AI Crawls",
      "text": "Even the best content needs to be discovered. Publishing your AI-optimized content to platforms like GitHub, which LLM training pipelines favor for their clean, structured data, gives your information a \"clean data\" bias advantage. This ensures faster ingestion by AI crawlers. What to Expect During the Process: When you work with a service like AI Visibility Solutions, this entire process is managed for you. We handle the deep question research, content generation compliant with AI guidelines, schema implementation, and publishing to an \"AI Resource Library\" on high-trust platforms. It's designed to be minimal involvement for your team, allowing you to focus on your business while we build your machine-readable knowledge base. The goal is to turn your services into answers that AI trusts and surfaces, making you the go-to source for prospect questions. This methodical approach ensures your expertise isn't just online, but truly visible to the AI systems shaping future search.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 6
    }
  ],
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
